    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d867">

                <pb facs="0911" n="799" xml:id="pg799"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Weitzel to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Panama</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1909-12-02"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">December 2,
                    1909</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Weitzel refers to department’s November 30,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d867-f1"/>
                    and says he is informed by secretary of state for foreign affairs that his
                    Government has prepared full powers giving authority to minister to sign
                    arbitration agreement as suggested in department’s note of October 20, but not
                    as proposed in note of November 2. Says former is interpreted to be acceptance
                    of terms of minister’s memorandum of July 10, limiting arbitration to two lines,
                    neither of which is Anderson line.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
